<title>USA: Federated Department to set $300 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Federated Department to set $300 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federated Department Stores Inc is expected to issue $300 million in two-part debt, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Baa2/BBB-minus rated deal is expected to include a 20-year issue and 30-year issue, putable in the seventh year, dealers said.</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co is expected to serve as lead underwriter for the offering, they said.</p>
<p>Federated operates more than 400 full-line department stores in densely populated urban or suburban markets in 33 states.</p>
<p>(( -- Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
